"peer_ticker":"QCOM",
"peer_disclosure_id":"qcom_2024_1A_D070",
"relationship":"related_topic",
"comparison":"Both companies cite competition and technological change as key risks in their respective PC/AI markets. AMD notes that 'increased competition' was a driver of past Client segment declines. QCOM similarly states that 'competition may intensify' as competitors expand offerings and reduce prices, specifically mentioning the 'demand for always on, always connected capabilities, the increasing use of AI and machine learning technologies' as a factor affecting competitive dynamics. While AMD focuses on the risk of declining revenue due to these factors, QCOM focuses on the risk to market share and pricing power.",
